1
00:00:00,510 --> 00:00:02,355
One manicure costs $60.

2
00:00:02,370 --> 00:00:03,495
Eight customers a day.

3
00:00:03,510 --> 00:00:05,920
Over $10,000 in monthly revenue!

4
00:00:05,970 --> 00:00:06,915
But in the end,

5
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:08,860
just $200 in operating profit?

6
00:00:09,090 --> 00:00:11,055
Here is the business concept.

7
00:00:11,070 --> 00:00:13,780
Break-even Point

8
00:00:14,010 --> 00:00:15,735
How much business does a salon need

9
00:00:15,750 --> 00:00:16,840
to avoid a loss?

10
00:00:17,310 --> 00:00:19,540
Assume 26 operating days a month.

11
00:00:19,770 --> 00:00:21,880
Eight customers, at $60 each.

12
00:00:21,990 --> 00:00:25,240
Monthly revenue: $12,480.

13
00:00:25,710 --> 00:00:28,095
Materials and technician commission

14
00:00:28,110 --> 00:00:29,440
cost $35 per customer.

15
00:00:29,550 --> 00:00:31,395
Only $25 per customer remains

16
00:00:31,410 --> 00:00:32,560
as contribution margin.

17
00:00:32,790 --> 00:00:34,635
Then subtract $5,000 a month

18
00:00:34,650 --> 00:00:35,740
in fixed costs.

19
00:00:35,970 --> 00:00:38,020
Operating profit is just $200!

20
00:00:38,490 --> 00:00:40,780
How many customers to break even?

21
00:00:40,890 --> 00:00:42,460
$5,000 divided by $25.

22
00:00:42,570 --> 00:00:43,900
The answer: 200 customers.

23
00:00:44,130 --> 00:00:46,815
That is about eight customers a day.

24
00:00:46,830 --> 00:00:48,400
to cover costs.

25
00:00:48,870 --> 00:00:51,195
Being busy does not mean profit.

26
00:00:51,210 --> 00:00:52,155
What really matters

27
00:00:52,170 --> 00:00:55,540
is how much each customer contributes.

28
00:00:55,710 --> 00:00:57,640
This is Business Through Data.
